WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.559
See empty room on a slide, and your instinct is to fill it.

2
00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:07.382
That instinct makes slides harder to read.

3
00:00:07.432 --> 00:00:09.508
White space is how you fix it.

4
00:00:10.508 --> 00:00:14.279
White space is any area without content, not just white.

5
00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:20.028
It focuses the eye, groups related things, and makes a slide feel calm and confident.

6
00:00:21.028 --> 00:00:25.496
To find space, delete repeated logos and decorative shapes first.

7
00:00:25.546 --> 00:00:31.140
Then move reminders into your speaker notes, the single biggest source of new space in most decks.

8
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.505
Before: seven bullets, two logos and a tiny chart.

9
00:00:35.555 --> 00:00:39.709
After: one point, one big chart, one supporting line.

10
00:00:39.759 --> 00:00:42.973
New customers doubled after we simplified sign-up.

11
00:00:43.973 --> 00:00:46.467
In a video, space matters even more.

12
00:00:46.517 --> 00:00:48.883
Viewers can't lean in or flip back.

13
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:54.330
Spacious slides stay crisp, give animation room, and leave the bottom clear for captions.

14
00:00:55.373 --> 00:00:58.854
With PowerPoint2Vid, your speaker notes become the narration.

15
00:00:58.904 --> 00:01:03.116
On Pro, a.i. turns uncluttered slides into calm animated scenes.

16
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:06.369
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

